---
description: Odoo version upgrades (17→18, 18→19, 19→20) — process and custom-code migration
alwaysApply: false
---

For upgrading an Odoo database or porting custom modules between majors, use:

- `@knowledge/upgrades/upgrade-17-to-18/SKILL.md` (+ `references/upgrade-process.md`, `references/code-migration.md`)
- `@knowledge/upgrades/upgrade-18-to-19/SKILL.md` (+ `references/upgrade-process.md`, `references/code-migration.md`)
- `@knowledge/upgrades/upgrade-19-to-20/SKILL.md` (+ `references/upgrade-process.md`, `references/code-migration.md`)

Two halves, both required: (1) the database upgrade via Odoo's upgrade platform (test request → validate → production), and (2) making custom modules compatible with the target version first. Make custom code target-ready before requesting the production upgrade; rehearse on a test database; keep a restorable backup.

Headline custom-code changes: **17→18** `<tree>`→`<list>`, `oe_chatter`→`<chatter/>`, kanban `kanban-box`→`card`, `check_access_rights/_rule`→`check_access`/`has_access`, QUnit→Hoot, `publicWidget`→`Interaction`, `ir.property`/cron `numbercall` removed. **18→19** `groups_id`→`group_ids` (+`res.groups.privilege`), `_sql_constraints`→declarative `models.Constraint`, optional `Domain` class, external API `/json/2` (XML-RPC/JSON-RPC deprecated). **19→20** `ir.model.access.csv`+`ir.rule`→`ir.access.csv` (ACLs and record rules merged into `ir.access`), public `read_group(domain, groupby, aggregates, having, offset, limit, order)` (`fields=`/`lazy=` break), `_table_query` removed, `_check_access` deprecated, tracking values removed, Owl 2→**OWL 3** (22 breaking changes), removed/merged modules (`base_vat`, `base_iban`, `stock_picking_batch`→`stock`, `website_sale_wishlist`/`_comparison`→`website_sale`, `hr_org_chart`, `hr_homeworking`, `delivery_mondialrelay`, `transifex`, `hr_work_entry_holidays`), external API (`db` service removed; XML-RPC/JSON-RPC deprecated → JSON-2), Python 3.12 / PostgreSQL 16, Field Service→Planning, payroll work entries removed. Support: 17.0 ended Sept 2026; 18.0 to Sept 2027; 19.0 to Sept 2028.
